     uummiiddii — USB MIDI devices

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     uummiiddii** aatt uuhhuubb??
     mmiiddii**  aatt uummiiddii??

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uummiiddii driver supports USB MIDI devices that follow the USB MIDI stan‐
     dard.  It also supports the following vendor specific devices:

           Roland UM1
           Yamaha UX256
           Yamaha UX96
           other Yamaha MIDI devices (hopefully)

     The uummiiddii driver is accessible through the midi(4) driver.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     midi(4), uhub(4), usb(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The uummiiddii driver appeared in OpenBSD 3.2.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     Some USB MIDI devices provide a switch for selecting between a vendor
     specific mode and standard USB MIDI mode.  Selecting standard USB MIDI
     mode may allow a device to attach as uummiiddii rather than ugen(4).  This is
     particularly true for Roland branded devices.

